Discover ING Hubs Romania

ING Hubs Romania offers 130 services in software development, data management, non-financial risk & compliance, audit, and retail operations to 24 ING units worldwide, with the help of over 2000 high-performing engineers, risk, and operations professionals. 
We started out in 2015 as ING's software development hub, then steadily expanded our range to include more services and competencies. Now we provide borderless services with bank-wide capabilities and operate from Bucharest.
Our tech capabilities remain the core of our business, with more than 1800 colleagues active in Data and Analytics Tech, Tech Foundation and Channels, Retail Core Banking and Architecture, and Global Products and Technology Services. 
We enjoy a flexible way of working and a highly collaborative environment, where fair and constructive feedback is encouraged. 
For us, impact isn't a perk. It's the driver of our work. We are guided and rewarded by a shared desire to make the world a better place, one innovative solution at a time. Our colleagues make it their job to do impactful things and they love doing it in good company. Do you? 
Here's a sneak peak of what our colleagues say about working within ING Hubs Romania:
• At ING, we're building the solutions of tomorrow, today | 80% of our colleagues in Romania agree

The Mission
The Compliance Frameworks & Policies team is part of the Group Compliance domain within ING within the Compliance Frameworks & Control (CF&C) department. The team plays a critical role in shaping and maintaining ING's global compliance risk management framework, ensuring consistent methodologies, tools, and reporting across all business lines and geographies. And supports the management of the global compliance function and its processes. The team supports the development, implementation and continuous improvement of global compliance frameworks, policies, and methodologies. It ensures that ING's compliance risk management cycle is effective, more data driven, and aligned with regulatory expectations and internal standards. The function serves all ING entities globally, enabling consistent compliance practices and insights across the bank. The role requires deep expertise in compliance and non-financial risk.

Your day to day
As Compliance Frameworks & Policies Specialist, you are part of global team responsible for designing, implementing, and maintaining ING's compliance risk management frameworks, methodologies and reporting. You will oversee compliance data driven reporting, and transformation initiatives. You will support the global Compliance function and functional processes to ensure efficient and effective functional management. You will work closely with stakeholders across the bank and regulators to ensure ING's compliance practices are robust, data-driven, and future-proof. This role is ideal for a specialist with deep compliance expertise and a passion for driving global change and continuous improvement.
Your key responsibilities:
In this role, you will contribute to the following areas: 
• Data, tooling and reporting: analyse and aggregate risk data, including RAC outputs, KRIs, issues and controls, and help translate complex data into clear risk insights, dashboards and management reporting;
• Tooling requirements and data quality: support the translation of business needs into tooling requirements, contribute to iRisk and reporting improvements, and promote a strong data quality and consistency mindset;
• Frameworks and methodologies: support the design, maintenance and improvement of global Compliance frameworks, methodologies and processes, including risk assessments, horizon scanning, risk appetite, policy governance and risk monitoring;
• Policy and framework implementation: help translate framework requirements into practical implementation guidance, training materials, awareness activities and support for Compliance teams across countries and entities;
• Stakeholder management: coordinate with global stakeholders across countries, entities, Compliance Risk Verticals and partner functions such as NFR, Integrated Risk, ODCR and COO Risk to ensure input, alignment and timely delivery;
• Regulatory alignment and internal control: help ensure that Compliance framework and governance arrangements remain aligned with regulatory expectations, internal control requirements and applicable ING standards;
• Transformation and simplification: contribute to global Compliance transformation initiatives that strengthen effectiveness, automation, consistency, scalability and forward-looking risk management. 

What you'll bring to the team:
• University degree or equivalent professional experience;
• Relevant specialist experience in Compliance, non-financial risk, risk management, data/reporting, policy governance or a closely related discipline;
• Good understanding of compliance or risk management frameworks, risk taxonomy, risk management cycles, internal control requirements and regulatory expectations;
• Strong analytical capabilities, with the ability to handle and aggregate large risk datasets, identify trends, spot emerging risks and translate complex data into clear risk insights;
• Experience with risk reporting, dashboard creation or management reporting, including the ability to develop clear risk narratives from data trends and root-cause information;
• Good understanding of risk management workflows and tooling; experience with iRisk GRC, Cognos, Power BI or comparable reporting and workflow tools is strongly relevant. 
• Ability to translate business needs into practical process, reporting or tooling requirements;
• Strong data quality mindset, including the ability to identify inconsistencies, challenge unclear information and propose practical fixes;
• Good stakeholder management and communication skills, with the ability to work in a global, matrix organisation across countries, entities and functions;
• Ability to take ownership of assigned deliverables, work independently, manage multiple concurrent priorities and remain effective in a fast-changing environment;
• Excellent verbal and written English. 

Nice to have:
• Knowledge of ING GRC tooling, iRisk workflows, Cognos, Power BI, data-driven reporting and/or portfolio analysis dashboards. 
• Experience analysing RAC outputs, KRIs, issues, controls, root causes or other non-financial risk datasets;
• Knowledge of ING's compliance risk management processes, including risk assessments, risk appetite, horizon scanning, policy governance, risk monitoring and compliance reporting;
• Familiarity with the NFR Framework, ERM Framework, Internal Control Binding Principles, relevant EBA standards and data governance expectations such as BCBS 239 is a plus;
• Exposure to process transformation, automation, simplification, AI-enabled tooling discussions or continuous improvement initiatives is a plus;
• Strong organisational understanding and ability to navigate ING's business structure, governance standards and risk ecosystem. 
• Curiosity, accountability, collaboration and adaptability, with the ability to challenge constructively, think creatively and improve ways of working. 
• Comfortable operating in a fast-moving environment with changing priorities, ambiguity and varying demands. 

If you want to deep dive into the processing of personal data conducted by ING Hubs Romania during the recruitment process and your rights related to it, read the privacy notices on our website (make sure to scroll until you reach the Data Protection section/ Candidates tab).

1571924fe707.description:
Responsibilities

We are looking within the Anti Money Laundering team for a Data Scientist in charge of the calibration of Financial Security Scenarios, whose function mainly consists of ensuring the optimization of the Group’s framework for fighting financial crime through its Transactions Monitoring Systems, by ensuring proper and correct calibrations of associated scenarios.

The calibration of a transaction monitoring scenario is the process of setting thresholds to target suspicious transactions or behavior. A scenario is a rule or algorithm designed based on the money laundering/terrorism finance risks associated with transactions or accounts, which is used to detect unusual transactions or behaviors by triggering alerts that are further investigated to detect Money Laundering/Terrorism Finance.

Thus, the role of the Data Scientist is to perform recurrent and ad-hoc studies of financial crime scenarios, reviewing their outputs, and setting new thresholds for their parameters.

Specifically, you will be required to:

• Calibration of Financial Crime Compliance Scenarios, employing statistical analysis and Group’s models.
• Data analysis: extraction of data, cleaning, analyzing, visualizing to support conclusions and support decision-making.
• Perform ad-hoc studies relevant for the optimization of financial security scenarios, the number of generated alerts.
• Analyzes the pertinence of generated alerts and proposes new thresholds ensuring operational efficiency of scenarios, as well as the quality of generated alerts.
• KPI reporting: Data recovery; Data consistency check (consistency of figures, monitoring of threshold variations, etc.), iterative work with the poles.
• Regular dashboard production and data analysis; Writing comments and drawing conclusions.
• Operational Committee & Annual review of scenarios: Production/Analysis of KPIs over the period; Preparation of the Operational Committee support draft.

Required

 Profile required 

• Good knowledge of SAS, SQL, Python, R;
• Statistical Analysis;
• Data analysis;
• Power Bi, Tableau or other Business Intelligence tool;
• Analytical thinking and ability to work with logical propositions and operators;
• English written and spoken level B2, good level of French;
• Knowledge related to Anti Money Laundering, financial crime detection or strong motivation to

evolving in this field is required;

• Good interpersonal skills, responsiveness, and ability to communicate with the central structure

located in another country, sense of service, flexibility;

• Efficiency, team spirit and ability to evolve in a fast and demanding work environment;
• Autonomy and sense of organization (management of priorities and deadlines);
• Graduate in Economic Cybernetics, Statistics and Computer Science, Banking or Computer

Science fields (Master or without);

• +2 years of relevant experience in statistics, risk modelling, risk scoring, AML calibration.

 Why join us 

Here, you will find a flexible workplace and culture, autonomy, constant learning opportunities, dynamism, and talented people, making this experience a real career accelerator. You will also discover all the diversity of our businesses, in a sector that is constantly evolving and innovating.

Plus, you will enjoy all our benefits:

• competitive compensation & remuneration, including annual performance bonus;
• preventive healthcare plan, and group health & life insurance;
• wide range of flexible benefits within a monthly budget;
• office perks, wellbeing and mental health programs;
• various social benefits and bonuses for personal or family events;
• 9-to-5 workday & flexible (hybrid) work environment;
• additional paid and unpaid time off, including Sabbatical leave;
• learning and growth opportunities based on individual development and career plans;
• unlimited access to various eLearning resources.

 Business insight 

We are convinced that people are drivers of change, and that the world of tomorrow will be shaped by all their initiatives, from the smallest to the most ambitious.

Whether you’re joining us for a period of months, years or your entire career, together we can have a positive impact on the future. Creating, daring, innovating and taking action are part of our DNA.

If you too want to be directly involved, grow in a stimulating and caring environment, feel useful on a daily basis and develop or strengthen your expertise, you will feel right at home with us!

Still hesitating?

You should know that our employees can dedicate several days per year to solidarity actions during their working hours, including sponsoring people struggling with their orientation or professional integration, participating in the financial education of young apprentices, and sharing their skills with charities. There are many ways to get involved.

